+#
+#	Drop the console drivers.
+#
+#	This build only ever serves the arcade pages: emuinfo.txt points the "fba"
+#	entry here, while the Mega Drive, SNES and NES pages each run their own
+#	emulator (md_emu.dge, sfc_emu.dge, fc_emu.dge) and the Neo Geo page stays
+#	on the stock fba029743. So FBNeo's console drivers are never reachable,
+#	and they are the largest objects in the build: d_spectrum 3.7MB, d_gba
+#	3.6MB, d_nes 3.0MB, d_megadrive 2.8MB, d_snes 2.6MB, d_msx 1.9MB.
+#
+#	Removing them is not only tidiness. The bridge that copies files to the
+#	card refuses anything over 30MB, and the device has 262MB of RAM with a
+#	driver scan at startup that touches every driver's name. Smaller is
+#	better on both counts.
+#
+#	Anything removed here must be checked against the 212 romsets the arcade
+#	pages actually list; dep/generated/driverlist.h is the authority on what
+#	ended up in the build.
+#	Note: d_sms.o has to stay - smsrender.cpp needs SMSPalette from it.
